# COMPONENT

## SmWorkflow

### DESCRIPTION

Run software-development workflows with Workflow-owned state, deterministic calculations and managed effects. GoalPhase, SplitPhase and RepositorySync expose named business Operations: Start creates an execution and returns sessionId; subsequent calls address that execution. Advance selects the next semantic Request, Human question, Wait or Terminal result. Submit consumes only the assigned typed result or answer and returns actual acceptance with useful chat text; it does not select the next action. Managed Workflow handlers own Git, SBT and other external effects, while the AI participant performs the requested semantic work. AI invocation and client round-trip reduction are explicit design goals, not measured performance claims. Shared Subsystem storage and configured host authority support these Operations. Declarations alone do not install handlers or grant consent; CLI/skill/client wiring is separate from direct Operation execution.

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.smworkflow

### COMPONENTLET

#### public-goal-phase-workflow

#### goal-phase-workflow-admin

#### public-split-phase-workflow

#### split-phase-workflow-admin

#### public-repository-sync-workflow

#### repository-sync-workflow-admin

