# SERVICE

## GoalPhaseService

### DESCRIPTION

Own the selected Phase's entry, assigned semantic/Human completion, mechanical progression, explicit validation and Step closure recovery and independently directed remaining-Plan adoption. The normal factory publishes startGoalPhase, advanceGoalPhase, submitGoalPhaseWorkResult, submitGoalPhaseOrderedDecision, describeGoalPhaseValidationRecovery, recoverGoalPhaseValidation, describeGoalPhaseSourceHistoryRecovery, recoverGoalPhaseSourceHistory, describeGoalPhaseClosureRecovery, recoverGoalPhaseClosure, describeGoalPhaseRemainingPlan and adoptGoalPhaseRemainingPlan. Session context resolves pending work and native state; callers supply business inputs or requested results, not control envelopes or stages. Configured managed Step/Phase checks, review, closure and repository effects retain their owning authority. Other declarations are not additional normal public stages. Accepted review or a Human answer alone does not establish committed Step, Phase completion or release.

### OPERATION

#### resolveGoalPhaseDiagnosticInformation

##### DESCRIPTION

Resolve one batched NeedInformation request against the exact currently issued RepairStep with retained failed-check context. Select failure-context, cause-chain, suite-context, execution-context, full-output or source-file with a reason. Retained logs are immutable; source-file reads use the managed repository File workspace and identify current observation with candidate applicability unverified. Empty selections restore a finite page of delivered Evidence references for a replacement worker; historyAfter continues that page. knownEvidence suppresses repeat payloads only for an exact retained batch already known to the caller. Persist requested facts and unavailable results in Common Evidence and its Journal producer. This operation neither completes work nor advances the Session, executes SBT, grants file authority or consumes repair allowance.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseDiagnosticInformationInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | GoalPhaseDiagnosticInformationInput | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseDiagnosticInformationResult

#### advanceGoalPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Advance the single execution identified by sessionId. Read native state/pending work directly and absorb managed mechanical progression. Return a typed Request, Human question, Wait or Terminal; work specifies submitOperation, submitSessionId and resultType. Internal RepositorySync work uses its own child session. The caller chooses no stage/Step/transition; only actual whole-Phase/repository completion is Terminal.

