# SERVICE

## SplitSemanticService

### DESCRIPTION

Required semantic SPI for only the unresolved inputs selected by SplitPhase
Workflow. Novel-work, partition and handoff-scope tasks have separate contracts;
the participant must return the result of the actual issued task, not choose
between these operations from a displayed stage. No semantic result grants
Human consent, storage access or command authority. Calibration, candidate
enumeration, validation, packing, ranking and progression remain Workflow-owned.

### OPERATION

#### assessPartitionSemanticInputs

##### DESCRIPTION

Answer the unknown-item and semantic-adjacency gaps in the exact issued
SplitPhasePartitionSemanticRequest. Return SplitPhasePartitionSemanticResult
with ordered requested estimates/boundary judgments, rationale and evidence,
or DecisionNeeded without inventing Human consent. Do not replace known-work
estimates, choose host identities, enumerate candidates or rerank results.
Workflow independently validates the data and owns deterministic calibration
and packing. The issued WorkOrder assigns the completion route; this Required
SPI is not an independent public planning or command operation.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhasePartitionSemanticRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhasePartitionSemanticResult

#### assessHandoffScopes

##### DESCRIPTION

Identify the evidence-producing and receiving scopes for the exact original
transfers in an issued SplitPhaseScopeSemanticRequest. Return
SplitPhaseScopeSemanticResult with exact ordered gap coverage, nonempty ordered
original-item subsets, rationale and execution evidence, or DecisionNeeded with
no partial scopes. Preserve ownership, closure obligations, transfer authority
and all retained candidates. The result supplies semantic data only and must
use the WorkOrder's completion route, not client-selected workflow operations.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSemanticRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSemanticResult

#### assessReasoningDemand

##### DESCRIPTION

Classify only the ordered unknown reasoning items in the exact issued
SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticRequest. Each item carries its original closure,
prerequisites and authority. Return ExpensiveReasoning or SettledExecution with
per-item rationale and evidence, or DecisionNeeded with no partial assignments.
Preserve known demands, source and authority. Do not select prices, policies,
replacement references, actors, commands, candidates or successor operations.
Use the WorkOrder's assigned completion route. The Required SPI declaration does
not install a reasoning participant or prove an issued native task. Copy the
Workflow-assigned request result identity/revision into the common result
envelope; do not select a destination or replacement data reference.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticResult

## SplitSemanticAdmissionService

### DESCRIPTION

Declare deterministic admissions associated with SplitPhase semantic Judgments.
Workflow reaches these admissions through the owning native call and complete
issued-result contract; an operation declaration is not a separately installed
public endpoint or an execution grant. Admissions check semantic data against
the original request while leaving all state changes and managed persistence
with Workflow. AI participants use their assigned completion route, not this
service to choose the next processing step.

### OPERATION

#### admitPartitionSemanticInputs

##### DESCRIPTION

Declare the local transactional admission associated with
AssessPartitionSemanticInputs and SplitPhasePartitionSemanticRequest. Workflow
validates exact ordered unknown-item/boundary coverage, preserved known work,
evidence and original authority before admitting SplitPhaseSemanticSubmissionResult.
The Judgment context is not a stand-alone client completion envelope, and decoded
data is not native execution provenance. Use the issued public completion route;
this declaration alone supplies no independently installed handler.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhasePartitionSemanticRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseSemanticSubmissionResult

#### admitHandoffScopes

##### DESCRIPTION

Declare the local transactional admission associated with AssessHandoffScopes
and SplitPhaseScopeSemanticRequest. Workflow validates exact gap order, original
item subsets, rationale/evidence and preserved whole-frontier authority before
admitting SplitPhaseScopeSubmissionResult. Ownership and closure are not rewritten
by a scope answer. This Judgment-context declaration is not a stand-alone public
completion handler; a skill must return the actual issued result through
submitHandoffScopeResult rather than select this admission or a successor stage.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSemanticRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSubmissionResult

#### admitReasoningDemand

##### DESCRIPTION

Declare the local transactional admission paired with AssessReasoningDemand.
Workflow consumes the one host-prepared current need and admits result context,
assigned reply, exact unknown-item coverage, classifications, rationale/evidence
and Workflow-selected output references at the semantic result boundary. It does
not compare complete source, closure or planning copies with the original request. Only
Workflow chooses replacement demand/planning references and resumes objective
selection. This declaration is not a separately installed completion endpoint,
native execution authority or an AI skill's permission to route processing.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSubmissionResult

