# SERVICE

## EvidenceService

### DESCRIPTION

Archive bounded released text batches, read common UTF-8 Evidence, continue retained Journal recording, and manage operational retention in the same host-configured collection and File workspace. Source associations grant no effect authority or test acceptance. Lifecycle and current payload availability remain separate.

### OPERATION

#### readEvidence

##### DESCRIPTION

Read a common Evidence by its public identity and optional revision. Return retained source/storage metadata and the currently available UTF-8 payload through the configured File workspace. Missing, unavailable and indeterminate payloads remain explicit; reading never repeats the original Test or repairs storage.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceReadInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | EvidenceReadInput | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceReadResult

#### recordEvidenceJournal

##### DESCRIPTION

Continue only the common Journal append for an Evidence identity with a retained actual storage observation. Return the existing Entry when already recorded, and keep Journal failure separate from Action and File outcomes. No archive write, Test, Workflow Submit or Advance is performed.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceJournalInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | EvidenceJournalInput | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceRecordingResult

#### archiveEvidenceBatch

##### DESCRIPTION

Archive 1 through 20 actual released source/output texts sequentially with identity or gzip representation. Keep each final source-associated destination before the File effect and return individual storage and Journal outcomes. Repeated or unknown writes are never replayed; partial batches are not rolled back.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceBatchArchiveInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | EvidenceBatchArchiveInput | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceBatchArchiveResult

#### describeEvidence

##### DESCRIPTION

Describe lifetime independently of current payload availability by public Evidence identity. Legacy rows without lifecycle metadata are unmanaged. Missing or expired text does not alter its historical Action, storage or Journal observation.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceDescribeInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | EvidenceDescribeInput | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceDetailResult

#### manageEvidenceRetention

##### DESCRIPTION

Track an existing allocation explicitly, hold tracked Evidence with a nonblank reason and canonical future reviewAt, or release a hold with a reason. A review date never releases a hold automatically. No caller can set completion or expiry, and no payload is deleted.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceRetentionInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | EvidenceRetentionInput | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceDetailResult

#### findDueEvidence

##### DESCRIPTION

Find finite indexed expiry or holdReview projections for the fixed host collection and specified repository, optional phase/session, limit 1 through 20 and exclusive Evidence identity cursor. Use the actual owning clock. Expiry excludes held Evidence; holdReview selects held records whose review is due. No full collection scan or automatic deletion is performed.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceDueInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| input | EvidenceDueInput | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

EvidenceDueResult

